            <ArticleTitle>Ovarian remnant excision necessitating resection of the anterior hypogastric system.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>235-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ovarian remnant syndrome is an unfortunate complication after bilateral oophorectomy. A case of an ovarian remnant involving the hypogastric vasculature is presented. Successful surgical management required resection of the involved hypogastric artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
